node.text:
{{emote|*mumbling*}} ...enough in this seam to meet quota, if those hewers don't ruin it again. Could have brought the whole place down with fissures like that...
{{emote|*You catch =subject.its= eye for a moment, but =subject.subjective= =verb:turn= =subject.its= whole body to face you.*}}
Ah! Wayfarer. I don't know your face, so you must be the new arrival. Come, I have a task that only you could be entrusted with.

{{emote|*=subject.T= =verb:hold= =subject.its= device-clad ear against the rock, as though expecting you to hear something too.*}}
It's like a heartbeat. A rhythmic pulse. I've heard centipede nests, aquifers, the very plates of the earth shifting, but never anything like this...
And I can hardly do my job with it drowning out every other signal in the rock. It would be irresponsible to keep them digging blind. But if we can't mine this seam, there's little chance we'll make quota, and we'll be kept here another cycle.
{{emote|*=subject.T= =verb:pull= away from the wall and =verb:place= a hand on your shoulder.*}}
You understand my predicament, yes, wayfarer? Good. I've recorded the pulse onto this disk. Take it to {{C|Grit Gate}}, and have the tinker-bears there inspect the frequencies encoded on it. With any luck, they can simply filter out the noise, and we can get on with our work.
